### Session 11 Lab: Library API on PostgreSQL (run with the IntelliJ HTTP client or VS Code REST Client)
@base = http://localhost:8080/api

### Paged search, filtered by author, newest first
GET {{base}}/books?author=orwell&page=0&size=5&sort=year,desc

### One author's books (JOIN FETCH, one query)
GET {{base}}/authors/1/books

### Create an author
POST {{base}}/authors
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Naguib Mahfouz" }

### Create a book for that author (use the id from the previous answer)
POST {{base}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Palace Walk", "isbn": "9780385264662", "year": 1956, "copies": 2, "authorId": 5 }

### Validation errors -> 400 with an "errors" map
POST {{base}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "", "isbn": "12", "year": 1000, "copies": -1 }

### Borrow: 201, due date = today + 14
POST {{base}}/loans
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookId": 1, "memberId": 1 }

### Borrow again: Sara now hits the max of 3 active loans -> 409 on the third try
POST {{base}}/loans
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookId": 3, "memberId": 1 }

### Sara's loans (book, author and member in one SELECT)
GET {{base}}/members/1/loans

### Return a loan, then try again -> 409
PATCH {{base}}/loans/1/return

### Delete a book that has loan history -> 409 (the foreign key protects the history)
DELETE {{base}}/books/2

### Delete a book that was never borrowed -> 204
DELETE {{base}}/books/6
